{"i":7,"result":{"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"id\": \"spec.json\", \"pointer\": \"\", \"view\": \"value\", \"value\": {\"format_version\": 2, \"case_id\": \"lie-module-irreducibility\", \"full_target\": \"Let \\\\(p\\\\) be any prime, \\\\(K\\\\) any field of characteristic \\\\(p\\\\), and\\n\\\\(\\\\lambda\\\\) an integer with \\\\(0\\\\leq\\\\lambda<p\\\\).\\nLet \\\\(V(\\\\lambda)\\\\) be the complex irreducible highest-weight\\n\\\\(\\\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\\\mathbb C)\\\\)-module of highest weight \\\\(\\\\lambda\\\\),\\nof dimension \\\\(\\\\lambda+1\\\\). Its Chevalley generators satisfy\\n\\n\\\\[\\n[h,x]=2x,\\\\qquad[h,y]=-2y,\\\\qquad[x,y]=h.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nChoose a nonzero highest-weight vector \\\\(v\\\\) with \\\\(xv=0\\\\) and\\n\\\\(hv=\\\\lambda v\\\\). Let \\\\(U_{\\\\mathbb Z}\\\\) be the integer subalgebra of\\nthe universal enveloping algebra generated by all divided powers\\n\\\\(X_r=x^r/r!\\\\), \\\\(Y_r=y^r/r!\\\\), for integers \\\\(r\\\\geq0\\\\).\\nAn **admissible lattice** \\\\(M\\\\subset V(\\\\lambda)\\\\) is a free abelian\\nsubgroup with an integer basis that is also a complex basis, stable under\\n\\\\(U_{\\\\mathbb Z}\\\\). It is arbitrary, not necessarily the minimal lattice.\\n\\nPut \\\\(V(K)=M\\\\otimes_{\\\\mathbb Z}K\\\\). The Lie algebra\\n\\\\(L(K)=(\\\\mathbb Zx+\\\\mathbb Zy+\\\\mathbb Zh)\\\\otimes_{\\\\mathbb Z}K\\\\)\\nacts by the induced lattice operators. This is the Chevalley\\n\\\\(\\\\mathfrak{sl}_2\\\\) construction also in characteristic 2.\\nProve that \\\\(V(K)\\\\) is nonzero and every \\\\(K\\\\)-linear subspace\\ninvariant under \\\\(x,y,h\\\\) is zero or all of \\\\(V(K)\\\\).\\nBoth \\\\(\\\\lambda=0\\\\) and \\\\(p=2\\\\) are included; \\\\(K\\\\) need not be\\nalgebraically closed.\", \"conclusion\": \"V_K is nonzero, and for every K-linear subspace W⊂V_K invariant under ρ_K(x⊗1), ρ_K(y⊗1), and ρ_K(h⊗1), either W={0} or W=V_K. Thus V(K) is irreducible as an L(K)-module, for every field K and every prime p and integer 0≤λ<p, including λ=0 and p=2.\", \"parameters\": [{\"symbol\": \"p\", \"type\": \"natural number\"}, {\"symbol\": \"K\", \"type\": \"field\"}, {\"symbol\": \"λ\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"symbol\": \"V\", \"type\": \"complex sl₂(ℂ)-module\"}, {\"symbol\": \"x\", \"type\": \"element of sl₂(ℂ), also denoting its complex-linear action on V\"}, {\"symbol\": \"y\", \"type\": \"element of sl₂(ℂ), also denoting its complex-linear action on V\"}, {\"symbol\": \"h\", \"type\": \"element of sl₂(ℂ), also denoting its complex-linear action on V\"}, {\"symbol\": \"v\", \"type\": \"element of V\"}, {\"symbol\": \"M\", \"type\": \"additive subgroup of V\"}], \"hypotheses\": [{\"id\": \"H001\", \"statement\": \"p is prime, K has characteristic p, and λ is an integer with 0≤λ<p.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:16-17\"}, {\"id\": \"H002\", \"statement\": \"V=V(λ) is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl₂(ℂ)-module of highest weight λ, has complex dimension λ+1, and its Chevalley generators x,y,h satisfy [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=−2y, [x,y]=h, both in sl₂(ℂ) and in their actions on V.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:18-24\"}, {\"id\": \"H003\", \"statement\": \"v∈V is nonzero, xv=0 and hv=λv.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:26-27\"}, {\"id\": \"H004\", \"statement\": \"M⊂V is an admissible lattice: it is a free abelian subgroup with an integer basis that is also a complex basis of V, and it is stable under U_Z. The lattice is arbitrary; it is not assumed to be the minimal lattice.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:30-32\"}], \"definitions\": [{\"id\": \"D001\", \"symbol\": \"n\", \"type\": \"integer\", \"definition\": \"n=λ+1.\", \"objects\": [\"λ\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D002\", \"symbol\": \"I\", \"type\": \"finite set of integers\", \"definition\": \"I={i∈ℤ:0≤i≤λ}; indices of finite sums and indexed families in this proof range over I unless another range is displayed.\", \"objects\": [\"λ\", \"i\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"i\", \"type\": \"integer\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D003\", \"symbol\": \"X\", \"type\": \"family of elements of U(sl₂(ℂ)) and their induced operators on V, indexed by nonnegative integers\", \"definition\": \"For every integer r≥0, X(r)=X_r=x^r/r! in the complex universal enveloping algebra U(sl₂(ℂ)); the same notation denotes its action on V. Powers are compositions on V, with zeroth power the identity.\", \"objects\": [\"x\", \"V\", \"r\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"r\", \"type\": \"nonnegative integer\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D004\", \"symbol\": \"Y\", \"type\": \"family of elements of U(sl₂(ℂ)) and their induced operators on V, indexed by nonnegative integers\", \"definition\": \"For every integer r≥0, Y(r)=Y_r=y^r/r! in U(sl₂(ℂ)); the same notation denotes its action on V, with zeroth power the identity.\", \"objects\": [\"y\", \"V\", \"r\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"r\", \"type\": \"nonnegative integer\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D005\", \"symbol\": \"U_Z\", \"type\": \"unital integer subalgebra of U(sl₂(ℂ))\", \"definition\": \"U_Z is the unital ℤ-subalgebra of U(sl₂(ℂ)) generated by X(r) and Y(r) for all integers r≥0, acting on V by its given sl₂(ℂ)-representation.\", \"objects\": [\"X\", \"Y\", \"V\"], \"depends_on\": [\"D003\", \"D004\"], \"requires\": [], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D006\", \"symbol\": \"e\", \"type\": \"family I→V\", \"definition\": \"For i∈I put e_i=e(i)=y^i v/i!.\", \"objects\": [\"I\", \"y\", \"v\", \"i\"], \"depends_on\": [\"D002\"], \"requires\": [], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"i\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D007\", \"symbol\": \"R\", \"type\": \"p-local subring of ℚ, with its usual inclusion in ℂ\", \"definition\": \"R=ℤ_(p)={a/b∈ℚ:a,b∈ℤ, b≠0, p∤b}, with the operations inherited from ℚ and its usual embedding in ℂ.\", \"objects\": [\"p\", \"a\", \"b\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [\"H001\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"a\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"symbol\": \"b\", \"type\": \"nonzero integer\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D008\", \"symbol\": \"M_R\", \"type\": \"R-module\", \"definition\": \"M_R=R⊗_ℤ M. Its elementary tensors are written r⊗m with r∈R and m∈M.\", \"objects\": [\"R\", \"M\", \"r\", \"m\"], \"depends_on\": [\"D007\"], \"requires\": [], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"r\", \"type\": \"element of R\"}, {\"symbol\": \"m\", \"type\": \"element of M\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D009\", \"symbol\": \"ι_M\", \"type\": \"R-linear map M_R→V\", \"definition\": \"ι_M(r⊗m)=r m, extending by addition from pure tensors, where R⊂ℂ and M⊂V. When its injectivity has been proved we identify M_R with its image under ι_M.\", \"objects\": [\"R\", \"M\", \"M_R\", \"V\", \"r\", \"m\"], \"depends_on\": [\"D007\", \"D008\"], \"requires\": [], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"r\", \"type\": \"element of R\"}, {\"symbol\": \"m\", \"type\": \"element of M\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D010\", \"symbol\": \"E\", \"type\": \"family I×I→End_ℂ(V)\", \"definition\": \"For i,j∈I, E_ij=E(i,j) is the unique complex-linear operator sending e_j to e_i and e_k to zero for each k∈I with k≠j.\", \"objects\": [\"I\", \"e\", \"V\", \"i\", \"j\", \"k\"], \"depends_on\": [\"D002\", \"D006\"], \"requires\": [\"N001\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"i\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}, {\"symbol\": \"j\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}, {\"symbol\": \"k\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D011\", \"symbol\": \"Π\", \"type\": \"complex-linear endomorphism of V\", \"definition\": \"Π=Y(λ)X(λ), with rightmost factor applied first.\", \"objects\": [\"Y\", \"X\", \"λ\", \"V\"], \"depends_on\": [\"D003\", \"D004\"], \"requires\": [\"H001\"], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D012\", \"symbol\": \"J_i\", \"type\": \"family of R-submodules of ℂ indexed by I\", \"definition\": \"For i∈I, J_i={c∈ℂ:c e_i∈ι_M(M_R)}. Scalar operations are inherited from ℂ.\", \"objects\": [\"I\", \"R\", \"e\", \"ι_M\", \"M_R\", \"i\", \"c\"], \"depends_on\": [\"D002\", \"D006\", \"D007\", \"D008\", 