{"i":2,"result":{"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"id\": \"source-map.json\", \"pointer\": \"/roots\", \"view\": \"value\", \"value\": [{\"id\": \"H001\", \"kind\": \"hypothesis\", \"statement\": \"p is prime, K has characteristic p, and λ is an integer with 0≤λ<p.\"}, {\"id\": \"H002\", \"kind\": \"hypothesis\", \"statement\": \"V=V(λ) is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl₂(ℂ)-module of highest weight λ, has complex dimension λ+1, and its Chevalley generators x,y,h satisfy [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=−2y, [x,y]=h, both in sl₂(ℂ) and in their actions on V.\"}, {\"id\": \"H003\", \"kind\": \"hypothesis\", \"statement\": \"v∈V is nonzero, xv=0 and hv=λv.\"}, {\"id\": \"H004\", \"kind\": \"hypothesis\", \"statement\": \"M⊂V is an admissible lattice: it is a free abelian subgroup with an integer basis that is also a complex basis of V, and it is stable under U_Z. The lattice is arbitrary; it is not assumed to be the minimal lattice.\"}, {\"id\": \"M001\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every division ring F, additive commutative group A with an F-module structure, finite index type Γ, and finite-dimensional F-vector space A, if f:Γ→A is F-linearly independent and |Γ|=finrank_F(A), then span_F(range f)=A.\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"LinearIndependent.span_eq_top_of_card_eq_finrank'\", \"hypotheses\": [\"F is a division ring, and A is an additive commutative group with an F-module structure.\", \"Γ is finite and A is finite-dimensional over F.\", \"The family f is F-linearly independent.\", \"|Γ|=finrank_F(A).\"], \"statement\": \"For every division ring F, additive commutative group A with an F-module structure, finite index type Γ, and finite-dimensional F-vector space A, if f:Γ→A is F-linearly independent and |Γ|=finrank_F(A), then span_F(range f)=A.\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Lemmas\", \"signature\": \"@LinearIndependent.span_eq_top_of_card_eq_finrank' : ∀ {K : Type u} {V : Type v} [inst : DivisionRing.{u} K] [inst_1 : AddCommGroup.{v} V]\\n  [inst_2 : _root_.Module.{u, v} K V] {ι : Type u_1} [inst_3 : Fintype.{u_1} ι] [FiniteDimensional.{u, v} K V]\\n  {b : ι → V},\\n  LinearIndependent.{u_1, u, v} K b →\\n    Eq.{1} (Fintype.card.{u_1} ι) (Module.finrank.{u, v} K V) →\\n      Eq.{v + 1} (Submodule.span.{u, v} K (Set.range.{v, u_1 + 1} b)) Top.top.{v}\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/FiniteDimensional/Lemmas.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"890800923ea50abc857f0ce470b4c689cc922d90259ef82fba0f39fa57681529\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"library/M001-0001/library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"8f774faf40d4998526e195603d193f6f47c6fb0251c72d3cc6305f7a4647e676\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"M002\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every commutative semiring R₀, additive commutative monoid A with an R₀-module structure, index type Γ, semiring S₀ with an R₀-algebra structure, R₀-basis B:Γ→A, and i∈Γ, the canonical S₀-basis B.baseChange(S₀) of S₀⊗_(R₀)A has ith vector 1⊗B_i. The canonical basis is obtained by tensoring the singleton S₀-basis of S₀ with B and reindexing Γ.\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"Module.Basis.baseChange_apply\", \"hypotheses\": [\"R₀ is a commutative semiring and A is an additive commutative monoid and R₀-module.\", \"S₀ is a semiring with an R₀-algebra structure.\", \"B is an R₀-basis of A indexed by Γ and i∈Γ.\"], \"statement\": \"For every commutative semiring R₀, additive commutative monoid A with an R₀-module structure, index type Γ, semiring S₀ with an R₀-algebra structure, R₀-basis B:Γ→A, and i∈Γ, the canonical S₀-basis B.baseChange(S₀) of S₀⊗_(R₀)A has ith vector 1⊗B_i. The canonical basis is obtained by tensoring the singleton S₀-basis of S₀ with B and reindexing Γ.\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Basis\", \"signature\": \"@Module.Basis.baseChange_apply : ∀ {R : Type u_1} {M : Type u_3} {ι : Type u_5} [inst : CommSemiring.{u_1} R] [inst_1 : AddCommMonoid.{u_3} M]\\n  [inst_2 : _root_.Module.{u_1, u_3} R M] (S : Type u_7) [inst_3 : Semiring.{u_7} S] [inst_4 : Algebra.{u_1, u_7} R S]\\n  (b : Module.Basis.{u_5, u_1, u_3} ι R M) (i : ι),\\n  Eq.{max (u_3 + 1) (u_7 + 1)} ((Module.Basis.baseChange.{u_1, u_3, u_5, u_7} S b) i)\\n    (TensorProduct.tmul.{u_1, u_7, u_3} R 1 (b i))\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/TensorProduct/Basis.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"ce068c65f80addfbf4d9d9e2849249f0811ccf5d04119beca1b111455401edc5\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"library/M002-0002/library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"891ec7ab54d25ae8d4f325a4bc023959560c0c2a3d576df581e2e3a9c529c7d8\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"M003\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every semiring R₀ satisfying the strong rank condition, additive commutative monoid A with an R₀-module structure, finite index type Γ and R₀-basis B indexed by Γ, finrank_(R₀)(A)=|Γ|. The strong rank condition means that an injective linear map R₀^u→R₀^w between finite free modules forces u≤w.\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"Module.finrank_eq_card_basis\", \"hypotheses\": [\"R₀ is a semiring satisfying the strong rank condition.\", \"A is an additive commutative monoid with an R₀-module structure.\", \"Γ is finite and B is an R₀-basis of A indexed by Γ.\"], \"statement\": \"For every semiring R₀ satisfying the strong rank condition, additive commutative monoid A with an R₀-module structure, finite index type Γ and R₀-basis B indexed by Γ, finrank_(R₀)(A)=|Γ|. The strong rank condition means that an injective linear map R₀^u→R₀^w between finite free modules forces u≤w.\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.StrongRankCondition\", \"signature\": \"@Module.finrank_eq_card_basis : ∀ {R : Type u} {M : Type v} [inst : Semiring.{u} R] [inst_1 : AddCommMonoid.{v} M] [inst_2 : _root_.Module.{u, v} R M]\\n  [StrongRankCondition.{u} R] {ι : Type w} [inst_4 : Fintype.{w} ι] (h : Module.Basis.{w, u, v} ι R M),\\n  Eq.{1} (Module.finrank.{u, v} R M) (Fintype.card.{w} ι)\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/StrongRankCondition.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"203821ca53dfd3aa7160b1c36fe2719275e7b0aac78a87e5aa9d87f0dd16fdc7\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"library/M003-0003/library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"0791a2de36eccf0d0a05c1605f61a6f54119719a017b1ac6e1d70370c8ac483e\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"M004\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every semiring R₀ satisfying the strong rank condition, finite index type Γ, and family A_i of additive commutative monoids with R₀-module structures, if each A_i is free and finitely generated over R₀, then finrank_(R₀)(∏_(i∈Γ) A_i)=Σ_(i∈Γ) finrank_(R₀)(A_i).\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"Module.finrank_pi_fintype\", \"hypotheses\": [\"R₀ is a semiring satisfying the strong rank condition.\", \"Γ is finite.\", \"Every A_i is an additive commutative monoid and R₀-module.\", \"Every A_i is free over R₀.\", \"Every A_i is finitely generated over R₀.\"], \"statement\": \"For every semiring R₀ satisfying the strong rank condition, finite index type Γ, and family A_i of additive commutative monoids with R₀-module structures, if each A_i is free and finitely generated over R₀, then finrank_(R₀)(∏_(i∈Γ) A_i)=Σ_(i∈Γ) finrank_(R₀)(A_i).\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions\", \"signature\": \"@Module.finrank_pi_fintype : ∀ (R : Type u) [inst : Semiring.{u} R] [StrongRankCondition.{u} R] {ι : Type v} [inst_2 : Fintype.{v} ι]\\n  {M : ι → Type w} [inst_3 : (i : ι) → AddCommMonoid.{w} (M i)] [inst_4 : (i : ι) → _root_.Module.{u, w} R (M i)]\\n  [∀ (i : ι), Module.Free.{u, w} R (M i)] [∀ (i : ι), Module.Finite.{u, w} R (M i)],\\n  Eq.{1} (Module.finrank.{u, max v w} R ((i : ι) → M i)) (∑ i, Module.finrank.{u, w} R (M i))\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/Constructions.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"395f49a423c4c46bb246eb11c785cbc350b3f938b1fa8b7e840635b208953e10\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"library/M004-0004/library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"ca6e36ce60385d3656402292744eedc25cbbb947eb996b050a14a0fb9fc8be58\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"M005\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every semiring R₀, additive commutative monoids A and B with R₀-module structures, and R₀-linear equivalence f:A→B, finrank_(R₀)(A)=finrank_(R₀)(B).\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"LinearEquiv.finrank_eq\", \"hypotheses\": [\"R₀ is a semiring and A,B are additive commutative monoids with R₀-module structures.\", \"f is an R₀-linear equivalence A→B.\"], \"statement\": \"For every semiring R₀, additive commutative monoids A and B with R₀-module structures, and R₀-linear equivalence f:A→B, finrank_(R₀)(A)=finrank_(R₀)(B).\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank\", \"signature\": \"@LinearEquiv.finrank_eq : ∀ {R : Type u} {M : Type v} {N : Type w} [inst : Semiring.{u} R] [inst_1 : AddCommMonoid.{v} M]\\n  [inst_2 : _root_.Module.{u, v} R M] [inst_3 : AddCommMonoid.{w} N] [inst_4 : _root_.Module.{u, w} R N]\\n  (f : LinearEquiv.{u, u, v, w} (RingHom.id.{u} R) M N), Eq.{1} (Module.finrank.{u, v} R M) (Module.finrank.{u, w} R N)\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/Finrank.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"4ab91c2b2e2d56f24c0260f25d55a31042cac8112a943a7c877594528c363e21\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"library/M005-0005/library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"5090aee0695da89d590a2b65b66e8141b17ffcae21a6bb19f23dcfbdf6001bc6\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"M006\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every pair of natural numbers u and ℓ, if ℓ is prime, then ℓ divides u! if and only if ℓ≤u.\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"Nat.Prime.dvd_factorial\", \"hypotheses\": [\"ℓ is prime.\"], \"statement\": \"For every pair of natural numbers u and ℓ, if ℓ is prime, then ℓ divides u! if and only if ℓ≤u.\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Factorial\", \"signature\": \"@Nat.Prime.dvd_factorial : ∀ {n p : ℕ}, Nat.Prime p → (Dvd.dvd.{0} p n.factorial ↔ LE.le.{0} p n)\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/Data/Nat/Prime/Factorial.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"caa753877be8d9ab5a656e6b95f9819dd590bda428e472749d6103423edf4993\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"library/M006-0006/library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"3cc1c94b98ca5427ba3fc645e055fa926ccb22dd3a5813c26fc557c4843d5ea7\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"M007\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every nonzero natural number u and every natural number ℓ≠1, there are natural numbers d and u' with ℓ∤u' and u=ℓ^d u'.\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"Nat.exists_eq_pow_mul_and_not_dvd\", \"hypotheses\": [\"u≠0.\", \"ℓ≠1.\"], \"statement\": \"For every nonzero natural number u and every natural number ℓ≠1, there are natural numbers d and u' with ℓ∤u' and u=ℓ^d u'.\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorization.Basic\", \"signature\": \"@Nat.exists_eq_pow_mul_and_not_dvd : ∀ {n : ℕ},\\n  Ne.{1} n 0 →\\n    ∀ (p : ℕ), Ne.{1} p 1 → ∃ e n', ¬Dvd.dvd.{0} p n' ∧ Eq.{1} n (HMul.hMul.{0, 0, 0} (HPow.hPow.{0, 0, 0} p e) n')\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/Data/Nat/Factorization/Basic.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"2b010d3541b123306d82df92d91491a0fe882342cc67e4d2b4408bbd690d69a8\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"library/M007-0007/library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"6299f5085eed9342567c3ecdd8d13278db17939f02814e6f03b0c329e1b1831b\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"M008\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every division ring F, additive commutative group A with an F-module structure, and finite subset B⊂A, the subspace span_F(B) is finite-dimensional over F.\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite\", \"hypotheses\": [\"F is a division ring and A is an additive commutative group with an F-module structure.\", \"B is a finite subset of A.\"], \"statement\": \"For every division ring F, additive commutative group A with an F-module structure, and finite subset B⊂A, the subspace span_F(B) is finite-dimensional over F.\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Defs\", \"signature\": \"@FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite : ∀ (K : Type u) {V : Type v} [inst : DivisionRing.{u} K] [inst_1 : AddCommGroup.{v} V]\\n  [inst_2 : _root_.Module.{u, v} K V] {A : Set.{v} V},\\n  Set.Finite.{v} A → FiniteDimensional.{u, v} K ↥(Submodule.span.{u, v} K A)\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/FiniteDimensional/Defs.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"67670bab4c51b4b7efa21232d77b5c52bbbf9213bd09277f9e640149edf34003\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"library/M008-0008/library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"18e8054e33e45ac2528f78d010f52f33dc54badf6927d7ef438d091c50a37fe4\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"M009\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"statement\": \"For every division ring F and additive commutative group A with an F-module structure, A is a free F-module (equivalently, it admits an F-basis).\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"Module.Free.of_divisionRing\", \"hypotheses\": [\"F is a division ring.\", \"A is an additive commutative group with an F-module structure.\"], \"statement\": \"For every division ring F and additive commutative group A with an F-module structure, A is a free F-module (equivalently, it admits an F-basis).\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.VectorSpace\", \"signature\": \"@Module.Free.of_divisionRing : ∀ (K : Type u_3) (V : Type u_4) [inst : DivisionRing.{u_3} K] [inst_1 : AddCommGroup.{u_4} V]\\n  [in