{"i":5,"result":{"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"id\": \"background-supplement.json\", \"pointer\": \"/notes/R002\", \"view\": \"value\", \"value\": [{\"id\": \"BG001\", \"at\": \"/inference/argument/0/text\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"fact\": \"For the prime natural p of H001 and integers b,d with p∤b and p∤d, p∤bd. Thus the permitted nonzero integer denominators in D007 are multiplicatively closed.\", \"grounds\": [{\"location\": \"/inputs/0/statement\", \"reason\": \"H001 explicitly supplies Nat.Prime p.\"}, {\"location\": \"/definitions/6/definition\", \"reason\": \"D007 specifies integer denominators b≠0 with p∤b.\"}], \"justification\": \"The checked Int.Prime.dvd_mul' says (p:ℤ)∣bd implies p∣b or p∣d. Each alternative contradicts the actual denominator conditions; b,d nonzero also make bd nonzero. This fills routine prime-divisibility accounting in the displayed fraction construction, without importing a localization theorem.\", \"source\": {\"declaration\": \"Int.Prime.dvd_mul'\", \"module\": \"Mathlib.RingTheory.Int.Basic\", \"signature\": \"@Int.Prime.dvd_mul' : ∀ {m n : ℤ} {p : ℕ}, Nat.Prime p → Dvd.dvd.{0} (↑p) (HMul.hMul.{0, 0, 0} m n) → Dvd.dvd.{0} (↑p) m ∨ Dvd.dvd.{0} (↑p) n\", \"declaration_kind\": \"theorem\", \"source_path\": \"Mathlib/RingTheory/Int/Basic.lean\", \"source_sha256\": \"c35204fe93e22d960b9e0f1d04e2f2f5f2bf73b540a7e7fec0bfcf5bf1349499\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"review-evidence/reuse/9e2bbcb2883d9a4e6b8fe03340edcbc85a5d30f4110f98c450e77a0632149660-library-sources.json\", \"sha256\": \"9e2bbcb2883d9a4e6b8fe03340edcbc85a5d30f4110f98c450e77a0632149660\"}]}}, {\"id\": \"BG002\", \"at\": \"/inference/argument/0/text\", \"kind\": \"mathlib\", \"fact\": \"The index type of the simultaneous basis B chosen from H004 is finite when B is viewed as a complex basis of the finite-dimensional V.\", \"grounds\": [{\"location\": \"/inputs/1/statement\", \"reason\": \"H002 states that